# What stays out of Git under 5GSim.
#
# The per-run evidence trees Baseline/logs/ and Experiment_Cyber_Telemetry/logs/
# are re-included by the root .gitignore. The rules below then drop only the
# bulk output inside them, which any run regenerates from the manifest and the
# pose trace. The assembled datasets, pose traces, manifests, scalar results,
# scenario configuration, reports and notebooks all stay in Git.

# OMNeT++/Simu5G vector dumps and their indexes, about 2.2 GB across the two
# stages, up to 255 MB for a single 20-minute run. The scalar results (.sca)
# beside them are small and stay in Git.
**/*.vec
**/*.vci

# Raw per-flow metric exports, about 1.3 GB, up to 145 MB for one run. These are
# the bridge's input; its output, data/<run>_cosim.csv and the final dataset,
# is the deliverable and stays in Git.
**/logs/*_net.csv

# Simu5G itself is an upstream checkout built locally during setup, not part of
# this work. Experiment_Cyber_Telemetry/sim/Simu5G is a link into it.
/Baseline/sim/Simu5G/
